<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="024" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Add-file-to-running-chat prompt (new session vs add-to-current)</title>
    <phase>2 Session</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Client-only UX change (a two-choice prompt + branch on the file-attach path); no BFF surface, no architecture change — STANDARD.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified UI prompt + branch over existing `ConversationPane` file-attach; low ambiguity.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P2-ui</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Client-only, distinct file surface (`ConversationPane` file-attach) from the BFF session tasks; can run alongside them once 023 lands the two-tier model.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>023</deps>
    <tags>frontend, session</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    When a user adds a file to a live chat, show a two-choice prompt: "new session" (archives the current session,
    switchable back) vs "add to current session" (keeps the file in the current session context). Wire each choice to
    the correct behavior on the existing `ConversationPane` file-attach path, reusing the fork/archive seam from tasks
    021/022 for the "new session" branch.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the SpaarkeAi three-pane `ConversationPane` file-attach flow and Fluent v9
    dialog patterns. Follow ADRs strictly (ADR-021 Fluent v9).
  </role>

  <goal>
    Adding a file to a live chat presents a two-choice prompt; "new session" archives the current session (switchable
    back) and starts a fresh one with the file; "add to current session" keeps the file in the current session
    context; the client build is green.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      spec FR-08 (§3 #3): adding a file mid-conversation must not silently pick a behavior. "New session" reuses the
      fork/archive path (task 021 fork or the archive seam from 022) so the prior session stays retrievable; "add to
      current" simply attaches the file into the current session's context. This is a client-side prompt + branch on
      the existing `ConversationPane` file-attach; no new BFF endpoint (fork already exists from task 021).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/.../ConversationPane (file-attach path + prompt)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/ (existing file-attach handler)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/patterns/ui/choice-dialog-pattern.md (two-choice dialog)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="023" status="pending">Two-tier session model + archive/switch-back behavior the "new session" branch relies on.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: file-attach on a live chat. MUST show the two-choice prompt; "new session" archives the current session (switchable back from history), "add to current" keeps the file in the current session context — no silent default.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: the "new session" branch. Reuse the task-021 fork / task-022 archive seam; MUST NOT introduce a new client-side session store or fork logic.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">SCOPE: the prompt UI. Fluent UI v9 dialog + theme tokens; MUST render correctly in dark mode.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ConversationPane file-attach + two-choice prompt</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/choice-dialog-pattern.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-component-authoring.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="two-choice dialog" location=".claude/patterns/ui/choice-dialog-pattern.md">
        Use the established choice-dialog pattern for the new-session vs add-to-current prompt.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare STANDARD rigor + reason; load knowledge; locate the `ConversationPane` file-attach path.</step>
    <step order="1">Insert the two-choice prompt when a file is added to a live (non-empty) chat.</step>
    <step order="2">Wire "new session" → archive current (switchable back) + start fresh with the file (reuse task-021/022 seam).</step>
    <step order="3">Wire "add to current session" → attach the file into the current session's context.</step>
    <step order="4">Build the SpaarkeAi client; manual/scripted UI check of both branches + dark mode.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set 024 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="6">Document any deviation in projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Prompt appears on add-file to live chat">
      <steps><step>Start a chat with at least one message, then attach a file.</step></steps>
      <expected>A two-choice prompt ("new session" / "add to current session") appears; renders correctly in light + dark mode (ADR-021).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="New-session branch archives + switches">
      <steps><step>Attach a file, choose "new session".</step><step>Open history.</step></steps>
      <expected>A fresh session starts with the file; the prior session is archived and switchable back from history.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Add-to-current branch keeps context">
      <steps><step>Attach a file, choose "add to current session".</step></steps>
      <expected>The file is added into the current session context; no new session; no archive.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build the SpaarkeAi client.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/ (ConversationPane file-attach prompt + branches)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a live chat with prior messages, when a file is attached, then a two-choice prompt ("new session" / "add to current session") is shown.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the prompt, when "new session" is chosen, then the current session is archived (switchable back) and a fresh session starts holding the file.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the prompt, when "add to current session" is chosen, then the file is kept in the current session context (no new session, no archive).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: attaching a file does NOT silently pick a behavior without the prompt.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The prompt renders correctly in light + dark mode (ADR-021); client build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-08 / PLAN §2.5. Reuse the fork/archive seam from tasks 021/022 for the "new session" branch — no new client fork logic.

    === COMPLETION (2026-07-29, STANDARD rigor, sonnet/high) ===
    Two-choice `ChoiceDialog` (`FileAttachSessionPrompt.tsx`, new self-contained file — mirrors the
    task-023 "keep it out of `ConversationPane.tsx`" merge-order precedent set by `HistoryOverlay.tsx`'s
    "Promote to Analysis…" affordance) shown when a file attaches to a chat that already has messages
    (`chatMessageCount > 0`, tracked via `onMessagesChange`). Options: "Start a new session" / "Add to
    current session"; Cancel present (ChoiceDialog pattern) and applies NO default — dismissing just
    leaves the file attached-but-unpromoted (negative acceptance criterion).

    Files: `useAttachments.ts` (new `hasPriorMessages` dep; a not-yet-decided ready chip is excluded
    from the existing auto-promote effect via `excludedFromAutoPromoteChipIdsRef` and queued into
    `pendingFileSessionChoice`; new `chooseAddToCurrentSession` / `prepareFilesForNewSession` /
    `dismissFileSessionChoice` controller methods); `FileAttachSessionPrompt.tsx` (new); `ConversationPane.tsx`
    (moved the pre-existing `chatMessageCount` state up ~1400 lines so `hasPriorMessages` is available at
    the `useAttachments` call site; +1 import; +1 dialog render wiring `prepareFilesForNewSession` together
    with the EXISTING `handleNewSession` seam on the "new session" choice — no new session-switch logic).

    DESIGN DEVIATION (surfaced, not silent — directional steps mode): the task suggested reusing the
    task-021 `/fork` endpoint for "new session". Investigated and did NOT use it — `/fork`'s
    `AnalysisForkRequest.DocumentId` MUST be a non-empty GUID of an EXISTING `sprk_document` (validated,
    400 otherwise), but a file just-attached mid-chat is only a session-scoped upload-cache entry
    (`POST /documents` mints a random `Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N")`, not a Dataverse `sprk_document`) —
    there is no existing seam that synchronously turns a raw chat attachment into a real `sprk_document`
    GUID. Forcing `/fork` here would require NEW document-creation plumbing, which is out of scope
    ("MUST NOT introduce new client-side session store or fork logic") and a bigger risk than the
    2-4 hour STANDARD budget. Grep confirmed `/fork` has ZERO existing client callers (task 024 would
    have been the first) — task 021's own docs already flagged its DocumentId precondition as
    document-first-flow-shaped, not raw-upload-shaped.

    Instead: "new session" reuses the EXISTING `handleNewSession` seam (`clearChatSession()` +
    `startNewSession()` — the same header "New session" button / task-021-era R4-5 mechanism) —
    genuinely no new session/fork logic. "Archived (switchable back)" is satisfied AS-IS: verified
    `ChatEndpoints.ListRecentSessionsAsync` → `SessionPersistenceService.ListRecentSessionsAsync` reads
    Cosmos and is NOT filtered by the Dataverse `sprk_isarchived` marker (task 022 already documented
    that marker as archival/advisory, not retrieval-gating) — so the prior session is fully retrievable
    from History regardless of whether the marker is durably flipped. The file itself is carried over:
    `prepareFilesForNewSession` queues the still-held `File` object (captured pre-remount); a new effect
    detects the moment `chatSessionId` actually switches to the freshly-minted session and POSTs the SAME
    `/documents` upload against the NEW session id, then settles the Event-path gesture via the EXISTING
    `fireForPromotedFile` synthetic-batch seam (`useEventBatch.ts`) that `spaarkeai-compose-r2`'s manual
    Browse-ingest ceremony already uses for a file promoted outside the attachment strip — no new
    Event-path mechanism either.

    If a durable Dataverse-flag flip + Analysis anchor for a raw mid-chat attachment IS wanted later,
    that requires either (a) a "persist the raw attach to a real sprk_document" seam feeding `/fork`'s
    DocumentId, or (b) a `/fork`-shaped-but-DocumentId-optional variant — both are net-new BFF surface,
    out of this task's "no BFF change expected" scope; flagging for owner triage, not blocking this task.

    GATES (STANDARD — Step 9.5 skipped per rigor level): `npm run typecheck` (tsc-surface-gate) — 0
    surface-owned errors (291 pre-existing shared-lib errors deferred to Phase B, unrelated). New jest
    suite `ConversationPane.file-attach-session-prompt.test.tsx` — 7/7 pass, covering: prompt appears on
    live-chat attach; prompt does NOT appear on an empty/new chat (existing auto-promote unaffected);
    negative — no `/documents` POST fires before a choice is made; "add to current" promotes into the
    SAME session (no remount); "new session" archives-by-leaving-retrievable + remounts + carries the
    file into the NEW session only (never the old); dismiss applies no default; dark mode (`webDarkTheme`)
    smoke render. Full `src/components/conversation` suite (47 files / 426 tests) re-run green — no
    regressions. `npm run lint` could not run in this environment (ESLint v10 config mismatch,
    pre-existing/unrelated to this task — flagged, not fixed, out of scope).

    Merge-order: zero edits to `ConversationPane.tsx`'s JSX body beyond +1 import, +1 dialog block,
    +1 relocated `useState` — per the project CLAUDE.md merge-order note against
    `spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1`'s `ConversationPane` decomposition.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge files. Follow task-execute (STANDARD: Step 9.5 gates skipped).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
